{
  "dom_id": "step-q78568",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Consider a matrix equation $A{B}^{-1}\\,x=d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $5\\times 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $A{B}^{-1}\\,x=d$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{B}^{-1}\\,x & =d \\\\ {A}^{-1}A{B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}{B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${B}^{-1}\\,x={A}^{-1}\\,d$ by $B,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ B{B}^{-1}\\,x & =B{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}\\,x & =B{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & =B{A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
